rescuers in Thailand have brought all 12  members of the youth soccer team and  their coach out of a cave where they  were trapped for 18 days that's right  the last of the five people who were  still stuck underground were brought out  of the cave a short time ago and they  are being taken to a hospital you can  see the ambulances there the first-aid  boys are rescued on Sunday and Monday  are recovering this morning doctors say  they are in good spirits Anna Warner is  near the rescue scene in Chiang Rai  Thailand Anna good morning good morning  and they you know they couldn't have  done any better on this rescue what an  amazing effort that they've managed to  pull off here you know the world has  been watching this rescue mission for  two weeks  this whole these whole events in the  cave first wondering would they find the  team then once they were found wondering  how and if they could even rescue them  from the cave now today 19 divers went  in once again taking part to rescue the  remaining boys and their coach the team  will now undergo physical and mental  evaluations at the hospital they've been  trapped since June 23rd when they  explored the cave after soccer practice  and it was intense pressure to get these  boys out before heavy rains made this  dangerous operation even riskier divers  and consultants came from around the  world to help get the boys out including  the US Britain Australia China Japan  Finland and Belgium the boys in the  hospital they're expected to be there  for at least 7 days they're being  quarantined and two may have lung  infections but tonight we're learning  that the first the parents of the first  group of four boys actually have been  allowed into the same room with their  sons they had to stand two metres away  and wear protective gear like face masks  but they did get into the room with them  for the second group they have also seen  their boys but through a glass window so  that's good news for the parents has to  be a huge relief John  and a Warner in Thailand thanks a huge  relief indeed
 

